    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing, and the audit line confirms `membershipLevel=3`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string property with a `membershipLevel` integer property (`int32`, min 1, max 3, `readOnly`) with a description of the computation rule. This regenerates `OwnerDto` accordingly, so the response now exposes `membershipLevel` instead of `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `@Mapping` target and the `membershipTier(...)` method with `membershipLevel(...)`, which computes: start at 1, `+1` if an email is present, `+1` if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line (and its Javadoc) so it records `membershipLevel` instead of the tier.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreNumericLevel`) \u2014 a unique owner with an email yielding level `1 + email + namesake0 = 3` \u2014 passes.\n\nA note on one judgment call: the spec framed the create audit line as \"recording the tier,\" but in this codebase that line recorded `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate`, not the tier. I added `membershipLevel` to it to satisfy the spec's explicit instruction that the create audit line record the level. No test asserts on the audit content, so this is additive and safe.",
